<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Marley is a 32-year-old musician who comes for his yearly preventive visit, almost twelve weeks after digit-sparing excision of a stage IA acral melanoma of the right great toe. The graft has healed and he walks and runs normally. The ankle he sprained four weeks ago is nearly back to normal; he has run figures of eight without pain and played football last week in the ankle support. He has examined his skin and nails each month as taught and found nothing new. He is preparing for a tour and asks what he needs before he travels. He has no symptoms. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 32</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Stage IA acral melanoma of the right great toe, treated by digit-sparing excision; under surveillance</td></tr><tr><td>Recent illness</td><td>Right ankle sprain four weeks ago, nearly healed</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Plans</td><td>A tour starting next month</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on a tablet in the waiting room and reviewed with him by Dr. Clarke. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Very good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Supported by his family, his band and his faith community; looking forward to touring</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Does not smoke tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>Drinks alcohol rarely (AUDIT-C 1); single-question drug screen negative for unhealthy drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Runs most mornings; football twice a week</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals with fruit and vegetables daily</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven hours; shorter on tour</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>No new partners; no concerns</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt; no firearm at home</td></tr><tr><td>Oral health</td><td>Dental check six months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Uses earplugs on stage; no hearing or vision concerns</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

