    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated for a fit man of 32. One-time HIV and hepatitis C screening and hepatitis B screening are due; hepatitis B vaccination is recommended for adults under 60 and started today. Travel advice for the tour: a travel clinic visit if any destination needs other vaccines. [S]<list><item>HIV, hepatitis C antibody, and hepatitis B triple panel drawn today.</item><item>Influenza, COVID-19, and hepatitis B (dose 1 of 2) vaccines given today; hepatitis B dose 2 in one month.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acral melanoma of the right great toe, stage IA, after digit-sparing excision (C43.71)</content>. No sign of recurrence on full skin and node examination; self-examination going well. [S]<list><item>Keep monthly self-examination on tour, including the soles and nails.</item><item>Melanoma review next month as planned.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Lateral sprain of the right ankle (S93.401A)</content>. Nearly healed; balance slightly reduced on the right. [S]<list><item>Single-leg balance exercises daily; ankle support for football for three more months.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>120/74 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 1</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy drug use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Single-question screen negative for unhealthy drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Does not smoke tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No previous test on record; once-in-a-lifetime test drawn today with his agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No previous test on record; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening and vaccination</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Triple panel drawn today, as recommended for all adults; vaccination started today because there is no record of it</td></tr><tr><td>Skin cancer surveillance</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Full skin examination today; under melanoma surveillance with a yearly dermatology examination; screening recommendations for the general population do not apply to a person who has had melanoma</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Age 32, BMI 22.9, normal blood pressure, and no other risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Inactivated vaccine given before the tour</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>This season&apos;s mRNA vaccine given</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap six years ago; booster due in four years</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing protection</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Uses earplugs and in-ear monitors on stage; advised to keep doing so</td></tr><tr><td>Dental examination</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Six months ago</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, this season (inactivated); COVID-19 mRNA vaccine, this season&apos;s formula; Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Melanoma: Cutaneous, Version 3.2026 (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Screening and Testing for Hepatitis B Virus Infection: CDC Recommendations, United States, 2023 (2023); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: HIV, hepatitis B, and hepatitis C results at the melanoma review next month, with the second hepatitis B vaccine dose. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-19: three-month melanoma review: graft, nodes, full skin and nail examination, and self-examination. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
